WEBVTT

00:20:57.917 --> 00:21:00.184
I think what's really important
is to talk about

00:21:00.208 --> 00:21:03.768
how we build trust,
what we do with breaches of trust,

00:21:03.792 --> 00:21:06.768
and can we rebuild trust once it's broken?

00:21:06.792 --> 00:21:10.476
Because I do think
that at the time when people lived

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:15.476
in more traditional
structures in societies,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:19.101
and you kind of -- there's
always been breaches of trust.

00:21:19.125 --> 00:21:20.768
It's not like this is a new story.

00:21:20.792 --> 00:21:24.976
But when things are clearer
and you have clear expectations

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.268
and you know the hierarchy

00:21:26.292 --> 00:21:28.934
and you know what is
the role of the father, the mother,

00:21:28.958 --> 00:21:30.643
the children, the bosses,